    "## 3. Train / Test split strategy — subject-wise, not random\n",
    "\n",
    "This is one of the most important methodological decisions in this project. A **random** split\n",
    "over windows would put windows from the same person in both train and test — since consecutive\n",
    "overlapping windows are highly similar, and even non-overlapping windows from the same subject\n",
    "share that person's gait signature and sensor placement quirks, a random split leaks information\n",
    "and inflates test accuracy in a way that will **not** hold up on a new person wearing the sensors.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead, we hold out entire subjects for testing: the model never sees a single window from a\n",
    "test subject during training. This is the scientifically honest way to evaluate a HAR model\n",
    "intended to generalize to new users."
   ]
