    "## 4. Feature extraction (for classical ML)\n",
    "\n",
    "For each window we compute, per accelerometer axis (6 axes total: back_x/y/z, thigh_x/y/z):\n",
    "- **Time domain:** mean, std, min, max, median, IQR, skewness, kurtosis, RMS, zero-crossing rate\n",
    "- **Frequency domain:** dominant frequency and spectral energy (via FFT)\n",
    "\n",
    "Plus cross-axis features: Signal Magnitude Area (SMA) per sensor, and correlation between axis\n",
    "pairs on the same sensor. This gives an 80-dimensional feature vector per window — small enough\n",
    "for gradient-boosted trees, but rich enough to capture both the shape and the periodicity of the\n",
    "signal."
   ]
